cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GRAACE-Sim in your research, please cite it using the following metadata."
title: "GRAACE-Sim"
type: software
version: 0.2.1
license: GPL-3.0-or-later

authors:
  - given-names: Alex
    family-names: Long
    affiliation: Los Alamos National Laboratory

abstract: >
  GRAACE-Sim is a modular, reusable simulation framework for Prompt Gamma Activation Analysis (PGAA) and neutron activation analysis, pairing a compiled particle-transport engine (GEANT4) with a Python configuration layer. Strict schema validation, built-in catalogs of detectors and materials, and custom configuration files make simulations easy to set up, configure, and reproduce.

repository-code: "https://github.com/lanl/graace-sim"

keywords:
  - GEANT4
  - prompt gamma activation analysis
  - PGAA
  - neutron activation analysis
  - gamma spectroscopy
  - Monte Carlo simulation
